    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d869">

                <pb facs="0970" n="960" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg960"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1161 Johnston, Eric/3: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-12">April 12,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received April 13—4:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1269. Moscow papers for April 12 carried a Tass<anchor n="52" xml:id="d869-f1"/>
                    report London containing a statement of Mr. Eric Johnston to the effect that he
                    was going to Russia to discuss future trade possibilities with the Soviet Union
                    and to find out how the postwar position of Russia and its trade will affect the
                    average United States citizen. Tass quotes Mr. Johnston as stating that he
                    intended to speak frankly to the Russians, that he hoped they would speak
                    frankly with him and that he intended to study the economic consequences of the
                    differences in the social, political and economic systems of Russia and the
                    United States since if “we wish to have peace we must learn how to cooperate
                    together”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d869-f1" n="52" xml:id="d869-f1-content">
